   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8d2fb338-5322-4872-9b76-1976322cf56e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "This example has the same file structure as the previous static global data example.\n",
    "The computations carried out in [`compute.c`](./C/3_device_routine_wdynglobaldata/0_device_routine_wdynglobaldata_portyourself/compute.c) and [`device_routine.c`](./C/3_device_routine_wdynglobaldata/0_device_routine_wdynglobaldata_portyourself/device_routine.c) are identical, but there are some changes to the format of the global data.\n",
    "If you inspect [`global_data.c`](./C/3_device_routine_wdynglobaldata/0_device_routine_wdynglobaldata_portyourself/global_data.c), you will notice that instead of a statically allocated array, `constants` is now dynamically allocated to the size `isize`, with elements filled at definition.\n",
    "This definition is then carried out in [`device_routine.c`](./C/3_device_routine_wdynglobaldata/0_device_routine_wdynglobaldata_portyourself/device_routine.c).\n",
    "\n",
    "Take some time to study and understand the code before compiling and running it in its native CPU form below:"
